# Rust contract: collapsing model providers onto the host-CLI layer

## 1. Dependency edge: `derrick-models → derrick-tools`

**No cycle.** `derrick-tools/Cargo.toml` has no `derrick-*` dependencies — it is a true leaf (confirmed: only `async-trait`, `serde`, `serde_json`, `thiserror`, `tokio`, `which`). `derrick-tools` does **not** depend on `derrick-config` either, so the catalogue must be config-agnostic (it keys on plain `&str` host names, never on `Host`/`ModelDef`). The four crates that depend on `derrick-models` (`derrick-assay`, `derrick-cli`, `derrick-flow`, `derrick-adopt`) all already depend on `derrick-tools` or are downstream of it, so the new edge adds nothing to the existing DAG ordering.

Add to `derrick-models/Cargo.toml`:
```toml
derrick-tools = { path = "../derrick-tools" }
```

**What `derrick-models` imports from `derrick-tools`** (the entire public surface it needs):
- `HostAdapter` (the trait — for the boxed adapter object)
- `HostRequest`, `HostResponse` (request/response structs)
- `HostError` (for error mapping)
- `CopilotToolPermission` (to set `copilot_tools` on the request)
- The host constructors `ClaudeHost`, `CodexHost`, `CopilotHost`, `OpencodeHost`, and the new `AiderHost` — via `derrick_tools::hosts::*` or the re-exports
- `catalogue` (new module): `HostCatalogue`, or the free functions `catalogue::builtin()` / `catalogue::normalize(...)`

**`reqwest` can be dropped.** Its only consumers are `anthropic.rs` (`reqwest::Client`, SSE) and the `reqwest` header/error handling there. `openai_cli.rs`, `opencode.rs`, `subprocess.rs`, `shell.rs` use `tokio::process`/`shell_words`, not `reqwest`. Once `anthropic.rs` is deleted, `reqwest` has no users in the crate. `shell-words` should be re-audited too — it is only used by `subprocess.rs::parse_argv` and `shell.rs`; if `shell.rs` keeps parsing a configured command string it stays, otherwise it also drops. (Flag: verify `shell.rs` before removing `shell-words`.)

---

## 2. `derrick-tools/src/catalogue.rs`

Const-table, not lazy. The data is fully static (`&'static str` host names, model id slices, a `Copy` enum). A `match` on `host` returning borrowed `&'static` slices needs no allocation, no `OnceLock`, no `lazy_static`. `normalize` is the only function that allocates (it returns an owned `String` because it may strip a prefix). Keep it `pub` and dependency-free.

```rust
//! Curated host/model catalogue (May 2026). Single source of truth for
//! default models, `derrick models check`, and per-host id normalisation.
//! Owned by derrick-tools so both the in-crate adapters and derrick-cli can
//! reach it without a dependency cycle.

/// How a host CLI expects a `--model` argument to be spelled.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug, Eq, PartialEq)]
pub enum ModelIdStyle {
    /// Bare model id, any leading `provider/` is stripped (claude, codex, copilot).
    BareId,
    /// Fully-qualified `provider/model`, passed through verbatim (opencode, aider).
    ProviderModel,
}

/// Curated models for one host.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
pub struct HostModels {
    /// Host name, matching `HostAdapter::name()` and the registry key.
    pub host: &'static str,
    /// Default model id, or `None` for hosts with no curated default (opencode/aider).
    pub default_model: Option<&'static str>,
    /// Curated current model ids for this host.
    pub known: &'static [&'static str],
    /// How `--model` must be spelled for this host.
    pub id_style: ModelIdStyle,
}

/// The full curated catalogue.
#[derive(Clone, Copy, Debug)]
pub struct HostCatalogue {
    entries: &'static [HostModels],
}

impl HostCatalogue {
    /// Returns the entry for a host name, if curated.
    pub fn host(&self, host: &str) -> Option<&'static HostModels> { /* linear scan over entries */ }

    /// All curated host entries, stable order (claude, codex, copilot, opencode, aider).
    pub fn hosts(&self) -> &'static [HostModels] { self.entries }

    /// Whether `model` is in the curated `known` list for `host`.
    /// `false` when the host is unknown OR the model is not listed.
    /// Note: callers treat a `false` as WARN-not-FAIL per the hybrid-validation rule.
    pub fn is_known(&self, host: &str, model: &str) -> bool { /* ... */ }

    /// Normalises a model id for the given host's `id_style`:
    /// - `BareId`  : strip a single leading `provider/` segment if present.
    /// - `ProviderModel`: return verbatim.
    /// Unknown host: return verbatim (defensive; adapter still owns the final argv).
    /// Never translates dot<->dash (copilot keeps its dotted ids).
    pub fn normalize(&self, host: &str, model: &str) -> String { /* ... */ }
}

/// The baked-in May-2026 catalogue.
pub const fn builtin() -> HostCatalogue {
    const ENTRIES: &[HostModels] = &[
        HostModels { host: "claude",   default_model: Some("claude-opus-4-8"),
            known: &["claude-opus-4-8", "claude-sonnet-4-6", "claude-haiku-4-5"],
            id_style: ModelIdStyle::BareId },
        HostModels { host: "codex",    default_model: Some("gpt-5.5"),
            known: &["gpt-5.5", "gpt-5.4", "gpt-5.4-mini", "gpt-5.2-codex"],
            id_style: ModelIdStyle::BareId },
        HostModels { host: "copilot",  default_model: Some("gpt-5.4"),
            known: &["gpt-5.4", "gpt-5.3-codex", "claude-sonnet-4.6", "claude-haiku-4.5", "gpt-5.4-mini"],
            id_style: ModelIdStyle::BareId },
        HostModels { host: "opencode", default_model: None, known: &[/* curated provider/model */],
            id_style: ModelIdStyle::ProviderModel },
        HostModels { host: "aider",    default_model: None, known: &[/* curated provider/model */],
            id_style: ModelIdStyle::ProviderModel },
    ];
    HostCatalogue { entries: ENTRIES }
}
```

`builtin()` is `const fn` so the table is a true compile-time constant. Convenience free functions `pub fn is_known(host, model) -> bool` and `pub fn normalize(host, model) -> String` can wrap `builtin().is_known(...)` for the adapters that just want `catalogue::normalize(self.name(), model)`. Decide whether to expose both the method form and the free-function form — recommend free functions for the adapter call sites (terser) plus the `HostCatalogue` struct for the CLI which wants to iterate `hosts()`.

`normalize` strips exactly **one** leading `provider/` for `BareId`. Implementation: `model.split_once('/').map(|(_, rest)| rest).unwrap_or(model)` only when `id_style == BareId`. This handles `anthropic/claude-...`, `openai/gpt-...`, and any `provider/` for copilot in one branch; `ProviderModel` returns `model.to_owned()`.

