let hand_kind = hand_kind_for_executor(model.provider(), model.cli());  // line 598
```

**Resolution path:** executor_role (default "executor") → RoleBindings.get(executor_role) → ModelDef name → config.models().get(model_name) → hand_kind_for_executor(provider, cli) → HandKind → host name

**hand_kind_for_executor()** (lines 780–795 in steps.rs):
```rust
pub fn hand_kind_for_executor(provider: &str, cli: Option<&str>) -> HandKind {
    let matches = |name: &str| provider == name || cli.is_some_and(|value| value.starts_with(name));
    if matches("copilot") {
        HandKind::Copilot
    } else if matches("claude") {
        HandKind::Claude
    } else if matches("codex") {
        HandKind::Codex
    } else if matches("opencode") {
        HandKind::Opencode
    } else if matches("aider") {
        HandKind::Aider
    } else {
        HandKind::Human  // fallback
    }
}
```

This function is the **provider-to-HandKind mapper** — matches provider field OR cli field prefix against hardcoded names.

